{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b2c3d4e5-f6a7-8901-bcde-f12345678901",
    "name": "Mulat — Multi-Agent Troubleshooter",
    "description": "HTTP API for the agent service (FastAPI on port 8000 per architecture doc).\n\n**Import:** Postman → Import → select this file and `mulat-local.postman_environment.json`, then choose the **Mulat — Local** environment.\n\n**Flow:**\n1. Run **POST /ask** (or **POST /alert**). If the graph hits the human gate, the test script saves `thread_id` and `run_id`.\n2. Run **POST /approve** with approve or reject.\n\nThe **Tool backing APIs** folder calls Kubernetes and Prometheus directly (same endpoints as Tool_API.md) for testing RBAC and queries without the LLM.\n\nNote: The Python service is not in this repo yet; these requests match the planned contract in DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md and k8s-multi-agent-troubleshooter.md.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Agent API (mulat service)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET /health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
            "description": "Liveness/readiness once implemented (common FastAPI pattern)."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "GET /docs (OpenAPI UI)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/docs",
            "description": "FastAPI Swagger UI when the service is running."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /ask — full pre-release check",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200 || pm.response.code === 202) {",
                  "  try {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    if (body.thread_id) pm.environment.set('thread_id', body.thread_id);",
                  "    if (body.run_id) pm.environment.set('run_id', body.run_id);",
                  "  } catch (e) {}",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"Check the cluster before tomorrow's release.\",\n  \"source\": \"postman\",\n  \"thread_id\": \"{{$guid}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/ask",
            "description": "User/CLI trigger. Supervisor should fan out to all three specialists for a broad check."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /ask — node NotReady (node health only)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200 || pm.response.code === 202) {",
                  "  try {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    if (body.thread_id) pm.environment.set('thread_id', body.thread_id);",
                  "    if (body.run_id) pm.environment.set('run_id', body.run_id);",
                  "  } catch (e) {}",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"node-3 is NotReady — investigate disk and events.\",\n  \"source\": \"postman\",\n  \"hints\": {\n    \"node\": \"node-3\"\n  }\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/ask"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /ask — pod security scan (namespace)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200 || pm.response.code === 202) {",
                  "  try {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    if (body.thread_id) pm.environment.set('thread_id', body.thread_id);",
                  "    if (body.run_id) pm.environment.set('run_id', body.run_id);",
                  "  } catch (e) {}",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"message\": \"Scan namespace prod for PSS baseline violations and latest image tags.\",\n  \"source\": \"postman\",\n  \"hints\": {\n    \"namespace\": \"prod\"\n  }\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/ask"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /alert — Alertmanager webhook (NodeNotReady)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200 || pm.response.code === 202) {",
                  "  try {",
                  "    const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "    if (body.thread_id) pm.environment.set('thread_id', body.thread_id);",
                  "    if (body.run_id) pm.environment.set('run_id', body.run_id);",
                  "  } catch (e) {}",
                  "}"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"receiver\": \"mulat\",\n  \"status\": \"firing\",\n  \"alerts\": [\n    {\n      \"status\": \"firing\",\n      \"labels\": {\n        \"alertname\": \"KubeNodeNotReady\",\n        \"node\": \"node-3\",\n        \"severity\": \"critical\"\n      },\n      \"annotations\": {\n        \"summary\": \"Node node-3 is NotReady\",\n        \"description\": \"Kubelet on node-3 is not reporting ready.\"\n      },\n      \"startsAt\": \"2026-11-04T08:00:00Z\",\n      \"endsAt\": \"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"generatorURL\": \"http://prometheus:9090/graph\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"groupLabels\": {\n    \"alertname\": \"KubeNodeNotReady\"\n  },\n  \"commonLabels\": {\n    \"alertname\": \"KubeNodeNotReady\",\n    \"node\": \"node-3\"\n  },\n  \"commonAnnotations\": {},\n  \"externalURL\": \"http://alertmanager:9093\",\n  \"version\": \"4\",\n  \"groupKey\": \"{}:{alertname=\\\"KubeNodeNotReady\\\"}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/alert",
            "description": "Alertmanager webhook v4 shape. Route should normalize to the same graph entry as /ask."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /approve — approve report",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"thread_id\": \"{{thread_id}}\",\n  \"run_id\": \"{{run_id}}\",\n  \"decision\": \"approve\",\n  \"comment\": \"Acknowledged via Postman — no automated fixes.\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/approve",
            "description": "Resumes LangGraph after interrupt(). Uses thread/run ids from a prior /ask or /alert response."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "POST /approve — reject report",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"thread_id\": \"{{thread_id}}\",\n  \"run_id\": \"{{run_id}}\",\n  \"decision\": \"reject\",\n  \"comment\": \"Findings need manual verification first.\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/approve"
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Tool backing APIs (read-only, manual)",
      "description": "Direct calls matching Tool_API.md — use to verify ClusterRole before wiring agents. Set k8sServer and k8sToken in the environment (token from `kubectl create token` or kubeconfig user).",
      "item": [
